{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues","id":784983,"title":"[CofD corebook] How to run Investigations and Clues?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-12T14:26:06-08:00","id":784983,"title":"[CofD corebook] How to run Investigations and Clues?","content":"So, finally, we get the rules for making Investigation scenarios to run in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> corebook, getting the Clues and all. Only, I feel a bit confused by them. From mine reading it sounds like this:<br /> <br /> 1. Character are doing some actions to get <i>Clues</i>.<br /> 2. They get <i>Clue</i> with some <i>Elements</i>.<br /> 3, They can spend <i>Elements</i> to get more <i>Clues</i>.<br /> 4. When they are having enough <i>Clues</i> - <i>voila</i>, mystery solved! Characters get some epiphany and now have whole story. With one brillant light of understanding.<br /> <br /> The problem I have is in part of 2 and 3 I think - Where is &quot;we get Facts A, and B - so we are going for Fact C&quot; part of it?<br /> <br /> <b>How to run, for example, Abyssal Intruder research by this system? How could this all look like <i>in story</i>?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-10-2016, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T14:57:31-08:00","id":785004,"title":"","content":"I haven't gotten the book yet so I'm spitballing here but you rinse and repeat 2and 3 as necessary.<br /> <br /> Super ironically, it looks like OPP stole a march on FFG and made an RPG version of Arkham Horror. :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T16:07:14-08:00","id":785035,"title":"","content":"Sounds to me like a direct rip from GUMSHOE.<br /> <br /> Nothing wrong with that, of cours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T20:16:51-08:00","id":785143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues#post784983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, finally, we get the rules for making Investigation scenarios to run in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> corebook, getting the Clues and all. Only, I feel a bit confused by them. From mine reading it sounds like this:<br /> <br /> 1. Character are doing some actions to get Clues.<br /> 2. They get Clue with some elements.<br /> 3, They can spend elements to get more Clues.<br /> 4. When they are having enough Clues - <i>voila</i>, mystery solved! Characters get some epiphany and now have whole story. With one brillant light of understanding.<br /> <br /> The problem I have is in part of 2 and 3 I think - Where is &amp;quot;we get Facts A, and B - so we are going for Fact C&amp;quot; part of it?<br /> <br /> <b>How to run, for example, Abyssal Intruder research by this system? How could this all look like <i>in story</i>?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I'm not sure I totally &quot;get&quot; this system yet either; I'm a &quot;learn by doing&quot; kind of gal, so I'll have to use it to fully understand it. But from reading it, it looks similar to systems I've seen in other games. Actually, it reminds me a bit of Skill Challenges from D&amp;D 4e, but with better execution.<br /> <br /> Anyway, with your Abyssal Intruder example, you would first determine what exactly the players are trying to learn about Abyssal Intruders. Based on what they want to learn, you as ST set a number of clues that will be required to figure it out, with 1 being a relatively simple task, 5 being a very time-consuming task, and greater numbers being reserved for the kinds of mysteries that span whole chronicles.<br /> <br /> Once you've settled on how many clues are required, the players can begin trying to figure it out. You'll call for rolls based on how they are going about their research. So, if one of your players decides to hit the library, you might ask them to roll Intelligence + Academics and say it takes them a full day. If another character decides to tap their Occult contacts, that might be more like a Manipulation + Socialize (possibly benefiting from a relevant Contacts Merit) and take a couple hours at the most. Now, no matter the results of their rolls, they're each going to get a Clue. But that Clue might be incomplete, tainted, or come with an extra Element depending on the results.<br /> <br /> They can spend Elements for various dice bonuses related to their discoveries about Abyssal Intruders, and once they have accumulated the required number of Clues, they find the information they were looking for. However, if they have fewer Elements than the required number of Clues, there are additional complications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T22:48:30-08:00","id":785197,"title":"","content":"The Investigation system seems to be meant specifically for Very Meaningful Investigations, so you'd be hanging every Clue off a lot more than just a few random character actions. I think that the intent was to provide some explicit, but optional, rules for how to bring a previously significant tidbit back into play later on. So if you snip the discolored tail off a rat at one point because it's a Clue, you can later deduce that the machine in front of you is for producing poisonous gas. If you discovered some neat blackmail material, you can trot it out later on for a clear mechanical benefit when interacting with the target.<br /> <br /> It's not a system for plotting out your chronicle; it's a system for linking different scenes together to get equipment bonuses.<br /> <br /> I mean, it seems as simple as, &quot;Let's learn about ghosts. Oh, we have learned things about Moaning Myrtle. We just encountered Moaning Myrtle. I get a bonus to doing this thing with Moaning Myrtle because I learned about her earlier.&quot;<br /> <br /> I do see how the system is very vaguely written, which discomforts me, but considering the vast scope that you can apply it to, I can understand why it's so vague.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T00:01:16-08:00","id":785226,"title":"","content":"Okay, I have living example that is partially discovered by mine players to this day. Mine <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/706212-intruder-yellow-sign-hallows-as-stars?p=710293#post710293\">Yellow Sign Intruder</a> is Abyssal entity that lives in corrupted Ley Lines network ( Mandalas ) or weird XIX century theater play. I make for him write up to use with <b>Intruders</b> system of Research rolls, so we have material to show in live how could this work. Here it is...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Yellow Sign</span></b></span><br /> <b>Corrupted Mandala, Carcosa, City from Stars</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Research of Yellow Sign</b></span><br /> <b>Subject:</b> Yellow Sign / Carcosa Intruder<br /> <br /> <b>Capping Skill:</b> Occult<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended \u2013 30 successes. Dramatic Failure can give character <i>Illuminated</i>Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Research Times:</b> 1 day, 6 hours<br /> <br /> <b>Sources:</b> Hallows &amp; Ley Lines, City Planning, Astronomy, Niche Theatre Plays.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Modifiers:</b> Researcher is Initiated of Prime (+1), Researcher saw Yellow Sign (+1), (Other ideas? )<br /> <br /> <b>Successes<sup>1</sup> Information</b><br /> <br /> 0-2 Nothing<br /> <br /> 3-5 In dense human settlements, Hallows and Ley Lines make complex patters known as Mandalas. Most of the time they start to look like overlaid High Speech Runes. Those images can evolve with time, reflecting Resonance of the settlement.<br /> <br /> 6-9 There is known Mystery that makes shifts to the pattern of Mandala. It\u2019s starts with springing more and more Hallows, making them looks like star cluster Hyades. Time of spread is various to each instance of this phenomena.<br /> <br /> 10-14 Mystery in question is Abyssal Intruder that Guardians of Veil call the Yellow Sign or Corrupted Mandala. First name comes from the occult symbol that start to spread in the settlement where Intruder has shown. It is said to drive both Sleepers and Awakened mad with it, and more it\u2019s show on the city, the more people are mad. The more people are mad, the more Yellow Sign comes to be spread in the city.<br /> <br /> 15-19 In 1895 there was macabre and bizarre theatrical play written, called <i>King in Yellow</i>, from unknown author. It\u2019s full of Yellow Sign imagery and connected to \u201cLost City of Carcosa\u201d, located on the shores of Lake Hali in the Hyades. Those that read the original manuscript become totally obsessed with reenactment of the play \u2013 like the events in it were self-repeating history.<br /> <br /> 20-24 The rumor states that City of London has been burned by extremist Guardians of the Veil in Great Fire of 1666 because development of city started in Elizabeth II times summoned Yellow Sign and Carcosa in to reality. Awakened and Sleepwalkers were in the grasp of madness. Surviving Guardians has cleared memories of those events in those that lived and burn or destroyed any left documents on the subject.<br /> <br /> 25-29 If enough people were \u201cIlluminated\u201d and Hallows were Awakened, entity known as King in Yellow comes to the Abyss invaded city and start to prepare final ritual. He needs to put out larger part of Hallows and Ley Lines, to form giant Mandala of Yellow Sign over city. If he succeed, city moves beyond time and space, becoming Carcosa from the play.<br /> <br /> 30+ Only way to destroy the entity is to forget it \u2013 the Sign, the Hallows Mandala meaning, the play. So the cursed Logophages Legacy from Guardians of Veil are the cure for the Intruder endemic. At least until King in Yellow entity himself does been summoned in to reality \u2013 cause he can spread it\u2019s madness directly.<br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup> \u2013 For each 5 successes collected by researchers, Storyteller rolls 1 dice and adds one dice on each next interaction. If ST gets success, Logophagens from Guardians of Veil know that she studies the Corrupted Mandala and will try as soon as possible to get character, every here associates and <i>their </i>associates \u2013 to consume their memories and destroy every of her notes.<br /> <br /> <b>Illuminated [ Permanent ]</b><br /> Character has been \u201cIlluminated\u201d by the Yellow Sign. He wants to re-enact King in Yellow play ( even if she does not know about her ). She dreams about Carcosa and visages of King in Yellow. She unconsciously draw Yellow Sign.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Character completely forget about anything connected to Yellow Sign or Carcosa.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Character is \u201cplaying her role\u201d in the King in Yellow play. Character makes Yellow Sign in place where other people can find it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Use of Yellow Sign in play</b></span><br /> For example, I have London rules by the <i>Visus Urbem </i>cabal, from Hierarch and his Provost. They are connected to City Planning and their gone from the Logophagens memory feeding several times now \u2013 each time Logophagens have told them what they done and cabal chosen to forgot about Yellow Sign for the good of London City.<br /> <br /> <b>How something like that can be used with new Investigation system? I'm most concerned with moment, in plot, of &quot;I get the Clue - so what does this mean to character&quot;.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-26-2016, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T00:22:39-08:00","id":785235,"title":"","content":"...I think the first thing you need to do is re-read &quot;No Hard Answers&quot;...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T00:44:41-08:00","id":785248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785235#post785235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I think the first thing you need to do is re-read &quot;No Hard Answers&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>When I read it, it's sums up &quot;<b>do not</b> preper anything, make something up at last roll&quot;. Which is totally contrary to make good mystery scenarios - as you need have villain, weapons, crime scene etc. Things that bind finally in to <i>source</i> of mystery, first event and motivations.<br /> <br /> Not to mention - you need to give SOMETHING for the players each time they get the Clue.<br /> <br /> /Irony:/ Or does me watching and reading for almost 30 years of mystery stories was wrong?<br /> <br /> From what I know about mysteries scenarios ( like <b>Castle</b>, <b>Sherlock Holmes</b>, large quantity of mine <b>Mage </b>games ) you need to give clues ( and mechanical Clues in this subsystem I assume ) that means <b>something in the story</b>. Some evidence, some rumor, some info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-13-2015, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T00:47:25-08:00","id":785250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785248#post785248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I read it, it's sums up &quot;<b>do not</b> preper anything, make something up at last roll&quot;. Which is totally contrary to make good mystery secanrios - as you need have villian, weapons, etc. Things that bind finally in to source of mystery.<br /> <br /> Not to mention - you need to give SOMETHING for the players each time they get the Clue.<br /> <br /> /Irony:/ Or does me watching and reading for almost 30 years of mystery stories was wrong?<br /> <br /> From what I know about mysteries scenarios ( like Castle, Sherlock Holmes, large quantity of mine Mage games ) you need to give clues ( and mechanical Clues in this subsystem ) that means <b>something in the story</b>. Some evidance, some rumor, some info.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, maybe don't use the Investigation system if you have definitive answers for your mystery? Since it's pretty explicitly the opposite of what you want?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T00:48:46-08:00","id":785252,"title":"","content":"Wait, so Investigation subsystem is not made to run mystery scenarios? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For <b>what</b> is made then? To make random stories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T04:11:38-08:00","id":785308,"title":"","content":"Wrong Elizabeth.<br /> <br /> Actually, not Elizabeth at all, but Charles 2nd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T06:23:25-08:00","id":785358,"title":"","content":"So having not run the system at all, here's my take on your question.<br /> <br /> First of all, it's not about research rolls (like discovering information about your Yellow Sign). Instead, assume the Yellow Sign is acting in the city, and there are certain clues to it's whereabouts. From here, you run the investigation much as you would, except that when players make a roll and discover some new information (through contacts or w/e), you also give them a little token that they can spend to get bonuses. One player is poking around the library and finds references to the old play (1 Clue), another player finds a bunch of cultists performing rituals to summon him (1 clue), whatever.<br /> <br /> They spend the clues, and you can present the information that the entity they're investigating is known as the Yellow Sign, and can be fought by making people forget it.<br /> <br /> In a sense, it's a way of chaining together disparate rolls in the service of an investigation through these clue bonuses and gathering enough bonuses for the answer. Before, these rolls may have still happened but remained unconnected by the <b>mechanics</b>, while you connected them through the story. I don't think this needs to really change the way you run the mystery. The No Hard Answers, to me, is more about not depending on your players to put the clues to gether in the exact same sequence that you imagined, but rather adapt what they're doing and what they're finding to how they're approaching the problem. But it all builds towards the same mystery you had imagined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/825-magiuspendragon","name":"magiuspendragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T10:49:23-08:00","id":785469,"title":"","content":"Testing how Investigation mechanics could play on the session, I prepared the Clues from previous Research rolls results. They are written in logical extension of one another, but can be uncover \u201cnon-lineral\u201d, like based on the rule No Hard Answers. Deeper understanding of Investigation system below.<br /> <br /> Clues list:<ul><li>In dense human settlements, Hallows and Ley Lines make complex patters known as Mandalas. Most of the time they start to look like overlaid High Speech Runes. Those images can evolve with time, reflecting Resonance of the settlement.</li> </ul><ul><li>There is known Mystery that makes shifts to the pattern of Mandala.</li> </ul><ul><li>It\u2019s starts with springing more and more Hallows, making them looks like star cluster Hyades. Time of spread is various to each instance of this phenomena.</li> </ul><ul><li>Mystery in question is Abyssal Intruder that Guardians of Veil call the Yellow Sign or Corrupted Mandala. First name comes from the occult symbol that start to spread in the settlement where Intruder has shown.</li> </ul><ul><li>It is said to drive both Sleepers and Awakened mad with it, and more it\u2019s show on the city, the more people are mad. The more people are mad, the more Yellow Sign comes to be spread in the city.</li> </ul><ul><li>In 1895 there was macabre and bizarre theatrical play written, called King in Yellow, from unknown author. It\u2019s full of Yellow Sign imagery and connected to \u201cLost City of Carcosa\u201d, located on the shores of Lake Hali in the Hyades.</li> </ul><ul><li>Those that read the original manuscript become totally obsessed with reenactment of the play \u2013 like the events in it were self-repeating history.</li> </ul><ul><li>The rumor states that City of London has been burned by extremist Guardians of the Veil in Great Fire of 1666 because development of city started in Charles II Stuart times summoned Yellow Sign and Carcosa in to reality. Awakened and Sleepwalkers were in the grasp of madness.</li> </ul><ul><li>Surviving Guardians has cleared memories of those events in those that lived and burn or destroyed any left documents on the subject.</li> </ul><ul><li>If enough people were \u201cIlluminated\u201d and Hallows were Awakened, entity known as King in Yellow comes to the Abyss invaded city and start to prepare final ritual.</li> </ul><ul><li>King in Yellow needs to put out larger part of Hallows and Ley Lines, to form giant Mandala of Yellow Sign over city. If he succeed, city moves beyond time and space, becoming Carcosa from the play.</li> </ul><ul><li>Only way to destroy the entity is to forget it \u2013 the Sign, the Hallows Mandala meaning, the play. So the cursed Logophages Legacy from Guardians of Veil are the cure for the Intruder endemic.</li> </ul><ul><li>At least until King in Yellow entity himself does been summoned in to reality \u2013 cause he can spread it\u2019s madness directly.</li> </ul>So we see at about 13 Clues in this Investigation. Mine players get to 5 of them to this day, as I see how story unfolds in our play.<br /> <br /> Looking more in to subsystem rules, <b>No Binary Rolls</b> is interesting to dwell in to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD No Binary Rolls</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Play with stakes. Maybe failure at a given stage means the protagonists still find their Clue, but the antagonist realizes he\u2019s being pursued. Maybe finding that Clue takes longer than expected, so the culprit can get away with another stage of his plan. A good investigation story needs to maintain momentum, lest it become frustrating.<br /> In this system, Clues offer dice advantages for later rolls. Failure doesn\u2019t inherently mean the Clue isn\u2019t uncovered; it just means it can\u2019t offer a dice benefit later. It\u2019s up to you to determine just why that is. Is the evidence tainted? Is there a mitigating twist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Antagonists showing up? Tainted evidance? This gives me some idea\u2026<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s look how 5 Steps of Investigation would work with mine Yellow Sign Intruder mystery:<br /> <br /> <b>Step One: Decide the Scope of the Investigation</b><br /> Counted 13 Clues and by the advices it would be about 7 chapters in mystery focus story. Truth be told mine players uncovered those 5 in two game sessions, half centered on this plot. But I help them with one at least, so maybe it was reflecting this 4 in two game sessions.<br /> <br /> <b>Step Two: Determine the Potential Clue</b><br /> Clues itself we have written above. Maybe can change a bit wording with each, but sence more or less is covered.<br /> <br /> <b>Step Three: Establish Interval</b><br /> Here we start implying the <b>Mage</b> setting. Chracters will need to find Clues in concrete circumstances, mostly by diving in Libraries of Orders or getting them from NPCs. Both will need to sweeten the pot for the other sides, so I think about make Clues as rewards in Social Maneuvering of those sources. As to how much time it will take \u2013 I say that each roll in correct Library will be about 2-6 hours, as I posted in previous version of this Investigation. Other takes on the Clues can take other time periods. The whole deal is to get to the sources that offer those Clues <i>in the first place </i>\u2013 it\u2019s the \u201cmeat\u201d of Yellow Sign story.<br /> <br /> <b>Step Four: Create Dice Pool</b><br /> The Dice Pools itself are relatively simple. Most will be Intelligence+Occult.<br /> I have only one problem with this \u2013 I have a hacker PC in our group that wants to solve everything by the Web Search. In-character is logical for this, but with this take I cannot show all those mage NPCs are committed to the mystery \u2013 those that have Libraries, secret knowledge, or could be witnesses to previous Yellow Sign intrusion. How to solve this with Investigation mechanics? In rules in this section are mentions some bonus and penalties \u2013 maybe make some harsher penalties for dwelling in to Web?<br /> <br /> <b>Step Five: Uncover the Clue</b><br /> Here we make the roll itself and resolve the rolls. The rule of -1 penalty by using the same Skill means that Computers and Occult will quickly come outside of use. Maybe it good \u2013 maybe PCs will need Academics or Expression to understand the twisted truths encoded in the King in Yellow theater play itself?<br /> <br /> Now to the roll results\u2026<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Negative Condition is obvious \u2013 character becomes \u201cIlluminated\u201d as shown below.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>This particular mystery is based on the being connected to madness. Beside Condition on benfit of search, character also get\u2019s \u201cIlluminated\u201d one.<br /> <br /> <b>Illuminated [ Permanent ]</b><br /> Character has been \u201cIlluminated\u201d by the Yellow Sign. He wants to re-enact King in Yellow play ( even if she does not know about her ). She dreams about Carcosa and visages of King in Yellow. She unconsciously draw Yellow Sign.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Character completely forget about anything connected to Yellow Sign or Carcosa.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Character is \u201cplaying her role\u201d in the King in Yellow play. Character makes Yellow Sign in place where other people can find it.<br /> <br /> <b>Special:</b><br /> For this particular mystery, there is also one extra rule \u2013 as Logophagens activly look for people dwelling in to madness of Yellow Sign. After uncovering each Clue, Storyteller rolls number of uncovered to this time Clues as dicepool. If roll gets success, Logophagens from Guardians of Veil know that character studies the Corrupted Mandala and will try as soon as possible to get character, every here associates and their associates \u2013 to consume their memories and destroy every of her notes.<br /> <br /> Finally, we should go to the Uncovering the Truth \u2013 but the rules are not clear here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Uncovering the Truth</b><br /> Once characters have the requisite Clues, they may Uncover the Truth. So long as they have the required number of Clues, this doesn\u2019t require a roll; they have pieced togetherthe puzzle. However, for every Clue short of the required total, the Storyteller adds one significant complication to the investigation. Some example complications are:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The culprit has plausible deniability.<br /> \u2022 The culprit has a viable escape plan.<br /> \u2022 The culprit has a hostage.<br /> \u2022 The characters risk legal consequences if they pursue the culprit.<br /> \u2022 The characters risk professional or personal consequences if they pursue the culprit.<br /> \u2022 The crime in question was a smokescreen for a greater<br /> conspiracy.<br /> <br /> If possible, use input that came from the players during the investigation to determine the results. This doesn\u2019t necessarily mean they get to determine the culprit, but they should be able to influence the finer details. After all, if they made hypotheses and assumptions during the investigation, and their efforts were successful, that should mean most of their theories rang true.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if PCs collect all 13 Clues they just know the whole story. But what with all: \u201cHowever, for every Clue short of the required total, the Storyteller adds one significant complication to the investigation.\u201d So characters can roll somekind Investigation ( Skill ) roll and pice the Truth with less Clues? Does this roll get\u2019s like -1 penalty for each Clue the PCs did not uncover? It\u2019s written <i>very</i> obscurely\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-13-2015, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T13:36:21-08:00","id":785542,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785252#post785252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, so Investigation subsystem is not made to run mystery scenarios? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For <b>what</b> is made then? To make random stories?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785197#post785197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a system for plotting out your chronicle; it's a system for linking different scenes together to get equipment bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>This system is in the <i>player</i> section for a reason. It has the same emphasis as the combat section, or the equipment section.<br /> <br /> If you want advice on how to plot, then read the ST section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785469#post785469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if PCs collect all 13 Clues they just know the whole story. But what with all: \u201cHowever, for every Clue short of the required total, the Storyteller adds one significant complication to the investigation.\u201d So characters can roll somekind Investigation ( Skill ) roll and pice the Truth with less Clues? Does this roll get\u2019s like -1 penalty for each Clue the PCs did not uncover? It\u2019s written <i>very</i> obscurely\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you just <i>read the rules</i>!?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785469#post785469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Some example complications are:</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u2022 The culprit has plausible deniability.</i><br /> <i>\u2022 The culprit has a viable escape plan.</i><br /> <i>\u2022 The culprit has a hostage.</i><br /> <i>\u2022 The characters risk legal consequences if they pursue the culprit.</i><br /> <i>\u2022 The characters risk professional or personal consequences if they pursue the culprit.</i><br /> <i>\u2022 The crime in question was a smokescreen for a greater </i><i>conspiracy.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's right there! You <i>just quoted it</i>. It's the <i>very next sentence</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T14:03:11-08:00","id":785555,"title":"","content":"I think what Hampster is getting at is that the Investigation rules only present one way to uncover the truth: by finding all the prerequisite clues. Ok, cool. But then there's a list of complications that can ensue if the players try to uncover the truth without all of the prerequisite clues... Ok... But how do they do that? By my reading, you <i>need</i> to have all of the clues to even attemp to uncover the truth. Unless I'm missing something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T14:16:58-08:00","id":785560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues#post784983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, finally, we get the rules for making Investigation scenarios to run in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> corebook, getting the Clues and all. Only, I feel a bit confused by them. From mine reading it sounds like this:<br /> <br /> 1. Character are doing some actions to get Clues.<br /> 2. They get Clue with some elements.<br /> 3, They can spend elements to get more Clues.<br /> 4. When they are having enough Clues - <i>voila</i>, mystery solved! Characters get some epiphany and now have whole story. With one brillant light of understanding.<br /> <br /> The problem I have is in part of 2 and 3 I think - Where is &quot;we get Facts A, and B - so we are going for Fact C&quot; part of it?<br /> <br /> <b>How to run, for example, Abyssal Intruder research by this system? How could this all look like <i>in story</i>?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>1. You need to define the event that prompts the investigation, that affords the characters with motivation (and Aspirations) to start digging.<br /> <br /> 2. The onus on the how and what they wish to learn are on the players. Some might want to perform social maneuvering to be allowed to enter the censor's personal library, for example. It depends on resources.<br /> <br /> 3. They spend elements to facilitate getting new clues, yes. If, in the example above, they get a clue from the library as to the next location to feature the intrusion or phenomenon, the story is moving forward.<br /> <br /> 4. That should be at the climax. Even if it is confronting the antagonist with him making the confession whilst holding someone dear to the character's hostage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T14:27:29-08:00","id":785566,"title":"","content":"<b>Charlaquin</b> is right - wording on <i>Uncovering the Truth</i> is illogical ( or just unclear ). In one sentence it says you solve by collecting all Clues. Okay, thats works, you dig up whole story. But <b>next</b> sentence it says you can &quot;guess&quot; the Truth, but with incomplete Clues, giving complications - but instead <i>giving</i> mechanics, it's just state complications, not <b>how</b> characters do this to &quot;get the Truth&quot;.<br /> <br /> As re-reading whole subsystem, I suspect that you can <i>Uncover the Truth</i> with less than all Clues by some Investigation (Skill) roll, but I'm not sure here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-10-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T14:35:06-08:00","id":785572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785560#post785560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The onus on the how and what they wish to learn are on the players. Some might want to perform social maneuvering to be allowed to enter the censor's personal library, for example. It depends on resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I understand, <b>Ephsy</b>, all your advices. I only write mine &quot;ST advice&quot; notes to those sections where and what <i>could</i> PCs do. Like remembering to recall Social Maneuvering rules for interactions before session or how much can take diging through Library take. I <b>do not</b> want to enforce on players &quot;you must do <i>this</i> and <i>that </i>way&quot; - maybe just make &quot;look everything in Web&quot; as not as optimal like looking for other mages to knowledge, as I want to explore Consilium's ties in and mages society. Just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T15:19:27-08:00","id":785590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785566#post785566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Charlaquin</b> is right - wording on<i>Uncovering the Truth</i> is illogical ( or just unclear ). In one sentence it says you solve by collecting all Clues. Okay, thats works, you dig up whole story. But <b>next</b> sentence it says you can &quot;guess&quot; the Truth, but with incomplete Clues, giving complications - but instead <i>giving</i> mechanics, it's just state complications, not <b>how</b> characters do this to &quot;get the Truth&quot;.<br /> <br /> As re-reading whole subsystem, I suspect that you can <i>Uncover the Truth</i> with less than all Clues by some Investigation (Skill) roll, but I'm not sure here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>think</i> the intention is actually that you do need to have the minimum number of clues to uncover the truth, but the complications arise based on how many <i>elements</i> you have left by the time you get all of those clues. Based on this quote from page 79:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once the characters reach the required number of Clues, they\u2019re able to Uncover the Truth if that\u2019s their goal. They can do so without any additional rolls if they spend a number of Clue elements (divided however they like) equal to the required Clues for the investigation. </div> </div> </div>I also like the risk/reward dynamic that this interpretation creates. You can spend Elements to help you get more Clues (or to help on other rolls related to the Clue), but doing so means that you might have to face future consequences when you finally uncover the truth, unless you make up for it by finding some clues with extra elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-13-2015, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T15:22:49-08:00","id":785593,"title":"","content":"OH, wow. Nice catch, that really does add a whole other layer to it. Awesome.<br /> <br /> I think I have a solid sense of what Elements a single Clue contains, but does anyone have any insight into how they would theoretically go about crafting Clues and their elements? I might be overthinking it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T16:04:22-08:00","id":785618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785593#post785593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OH, wow. Nice catch, that really does add a whole other layer to it. Awesome.<br /> <br /> I think I have a solid sense of what Elements a single Clue contains, but does anyone have any insight into how they would theoretically go about crafting Clues and their elements? I might be overthinking it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the advice under the &quot;no hard answers&quot; section covers this really well. Don't craft Clues or elements ahead of time. When a player rolls to find a Clue, ask them &quot;what do you find?&quot; then work backwards to figure out how the Clue the player described will help lead them to the truth (if you even have a truth worked out beforehand). This requires a certain amount of skill at improvisation, but what part of STing doesn't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T18:03:28-08:00","id":785657,"title":"","content":"I always found <a href=\"http://thealexandrian.net/wordpress/1118/roleplaying-games/three-clue-rule\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a> a good one about designing clues.<br /> <br /> I'm certain I'm not the only one who's had players overlook what I thought was a blatantly obvious clue and go mad dogging it after a throwaway description. I could see some issues with asking the players what the clue is but that does seem to be the way games are developing. I've long ago put aside the notion of the game being players versus storyteller, but I'm still hung up on the storyteller making up most of the story. I guess some of the character creation concepts, like Vampire's Ladder and Werewolf's Funeral do put a lot in the hands of the player, though, so this isn't exactly groundbreaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T21:04:15-08:00","id":785730,"title":"","content":"I have two question left to the Investigation subsystem - <b>Can a one Clue have more than one Element <i>on base</i>, without Exceptional Success?</b><br /> <br /> Like one Clue is killers shoe size. Other is murder weapon. Murder weapon is much more important Clue, giving you 3 Elements, contrary to Shoe Size, giving you 1 Element - or something like that.<br /> <br /> Also, if <i>Uncovering the Truth</i> works with collecting all Clues - <b>Can characters &quot;guess&quot; with Investigation (Skill) roll the rest, <i>without</i> all the Clues? </b><br /> Like they do 2-3 times in <b>Castle</b> episode - they collect everything they got for now on the blackboard and Castle makes wild theory how it should work, and then Beckett could agree with him sometime - only it leads to scene that they are wrong, but new Clue is shown then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-14-2015, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T21:44:18-08:00","id":785749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785730#post785730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have two question left to the Investigation subsystem - <b>Can a one Clue have more than one Element <i>on base</i>, without Exceptional Success?</b><br /> <br /> Like one Clue is killers shoe size. Other is murder weapon. Murder weapon is much more important Clue, giving you 3 Elements, contrary to Shoe Size, giving you 1 Element.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the character who finds the clue has a 4+ dots or a relevant Specialty in the skill used to find it. Also, &quot;some Merits or other variables.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785730#post785730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if <i>Uncovering the Truth</i> works with collecting all Clues - <b>Can characters &amp;quot;guess&amp;quot; with Investigation (Skill) roll the rest, <i>without</i> all the Clues? </b><br /> Like they do 2-3 times in <b>Castle</b> episode - they collect everything on the blackboard and Castle makes wild theory how it should work, and then Beckett could agree with him sometime - only it leads to scene that they are wrong, but new Clue is shown then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by the rules as written, but it seems like a reasonable house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T23:53:54-08:00","id":785801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785749#post785749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not by the rules as written, but it seems like a reasonable house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a tainted clue in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T02:14:17-08:00","id":785838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785801#post785801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a tainted clue in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand Tainted Clues are for making lesser number of Elements on Uncovering the Truth stage. You get Complications, but you still get all Clues needed.<br /> <br /> I ask about situation when you <b>did not</b> get enough Clues and make (possibly) some kind Investigation (Skill) roll to get the rest of the story you <i>did not uncover</i>. Let's call it for now <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=klyfibEp-ow\" target=\"_blank\">Castle Theory</a> Roll</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For example, in mine Yellow Sign Investigation PCs need to uncover 13 Clues. Mine players have now 5 of them. Is it possible to let them make Castle Theory Roll? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I suspect that all <b>not uncovered</b> Elements still would make Complications. So if mine players would now wanted to make Castle Theory roll, needing still 8 Clues, they will get 8 Complications even if Uncovering the Truth would be successful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-14-2015, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T02:55:07-08:00","id":785850,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty annoyed by how the Investigation System write up starts. Also pretty sure that most fans and actual readers of mystery genre would throw a book at a game master saying &quot;What did you find?&quot; in response to successful roll. Don't call the game &quot;tales of mystery&quot; if your advise on using mystery in play is &quot;make stuff up and/or put players in position to make stuff up&quot;. It's not a mystery, it's procedural police drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T03:00:25-08:00","id":785852,"title":"","content":"Except most troupes won't be conformed by cops or follow their procedures. Role-play isn't a book or a script.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T03:06:30-08:00","id":785856,"title":"","content":"I'm talking about genre difference between Mystery and Crime/Procedural drama. One is not like the other. Most of TV Shows portraying detectives are not mystery stories. Majority of Sherlock Holmes stories are terrible at being mystery while being good at creating literary portrayal of fantastical detective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T03:43:44-08:00","id":785874,"title":"","content":"So... Semantics. Ok then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T08:16:36-08:00","id":785987,"title":"","content":"It's just hit me -<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> If Elements from Clues are used to get new Clues quicker, it means that Uncovering Clue roll is <i>not at all </i>about <b>what</b> characters find, but <b>where </b>they know to find it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>From mine example:</i><br /> <br /> If our previous Clue was <i>&quot;Mystery in question is Abyssal Intruder that Guardians of Veil call the Yellow Sign or Corrupted Mandala. First name comes from the occult symbol that start to spread in the settlement where Intruder has shown.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Then Element from it can be used to point <i>&quot;In 1895 there was macabre and bizarre theatrical play written, called King in Yellow, from unknown author. It\u2019s full of Yellow Sign imagery and connected to \u201cLost City of Carcosa\u201d, located on the shores of Lake Hali in the Hyades.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> BUT Uncovering the Clue gives us <i>not</i> the info itself, but rather <b>where</b> to find it. So our PCs could get from Element to look in &quot;Strange Symbolism&quot; darknet database on net or to go to Guardians Symbols Expert in Consilium ( based on previous Clue context). STILL, PC will <i>not</i> know anything about 'Lost City of Carcosa' <b>until</b> they solve a problem in getting it - like going in to weird darknet forums or Social Maneuvering the Guardian NPC to let him talk it. From Uncovering the Clue they know <b>where</b> to look, not the info itself.<br /> <br /> Or at least it's how interpret this quotes from corebook:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t be afraid to add story framing to the search for a Clue. In our previous examples, maybe the monster left behind a dangerous contaminant the characters have to overcome to case the scene. Or for our wrecked ship, perhaps the characters have to traverse shark-infested waters to get where they need to be. If the characters perform particularly well in these efforts, consider offering bonuses to the effort to find the Clue.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-14-2015, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T08:23:40-08:00","id":785991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785838#post785838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For example, in mine Yellow Sign Investigation PCs need to uncover 13 Clues. Mine players have now 5 of them. Is it possible to let them make Castle Theory Roll? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do they have at least 8 Elements? If so, yes, but (5+8=13). If no, they don't have enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T10:44:02-08:00","id":786079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785590#post785590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I <i>think</i> the intention is actually that you do need to have the minimum number of clues to uncover the truth, but the complications arise based on how many <i>elements</i> you have left by the time you get all of those clues. I also like the risk/reward dynamic that this interpretation creates. You can spend Elements to help you get more Clues (or to help on other rolls related to the Clue), but doing so means that you might have to face future consequences when you finally uncover the truth, unless you make up for it by finding some clues with extra elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I'm a little uncertain here.<br /> A.) Pg 79 states that Uncovering the Truth without further rolls requires the expenditure of elements equal to the number of Clues required.<br /> B.) Pg 81 states that Uncovering the Truth requires a certain number of Clues.<br /> <br /> So, considering a &quot;three-clue mystery&quot;:<br /> <br /> A.) Page 79 'wins'<br /> * Spending Clue elements on rolls reduces how many are available to Uncover the Truth.<br /> * Three &quot;empty&quot; Clues (their elements spent finding the other clues or during play) <b>can't</b> solve a three-Clue mystery.<br /> * A single Clue with 3 elements to spend <b>can </b>solve a three-Clue mystery.<br /> (Would they still suffer two complications, because they're two Clues short?)<br /> <br /> B.) Page 81 is correct<br /> * Spending Clue elements doesn't matter because 0-remaining-element Clues still count as Clues<br /> * Three &quot;empty&quot; Clues (their elements spent finding the other clues or during play) <b>can</b> solve a three-Clue mystery.<br /> (Would they still suffer three complications, because they're three elements short?)<br /> * A single Clue with 3 elements to spend <b>can't </b>solve a three-Clue mystery. (It's just more useful for finding other Clues.)<br /> <br /> C.) Both:<br /> * Spending Clue elements leads to complications during Uncovering the Truth<br /> * You need three Clues <i>and </i>three elements to &quot;cleanly&quot; solve a three-clue mystery.<br /> * Three &quot;empty&quot; Clues (their elements spent finding the other clues or during play) <b>can</b> solve a three-Clue mystery, but you suffer three complications.<br /> * A single Clue with 3 elements to spend <b>can't </b>solve a three-Clue mystery. (Not enough Clues.)<br /> * A single clue with 3 elements, and two other &quot;empty&quot; Clues, <b>can </b>solve a three-Clue mystery &quot;cleanly&quot;<br /> <br /> What do folks think? C seems to be the most game-useful as it keeps multiple-element Clues from trivializing whole investigations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T12:32:19-08:00","id":786131,"title":"","content":"I'm leaning towards C, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T12:41:20-08:00","id":786139,"title":"","content":"Yeah, C. sounds like it makes the most sense.<br /> <br /> At the risk of asking the obvious, how would you guys handle this situation:<br /> <br /> A character decides that they're going to investigate the city councilor who may be connected to the case in accordance with a previously gathered Clue.<br /> <br /> He spends an action trying to secure a meeting with the councilor. Let's say this is Equipment or whatever that he acquires through his skills.<br /> <br /> He arranges the meeting and goes to talk to the Councilor, trying to use Social Maneuvering to give up the next clue. He opens one door, then in a fit of desperation, forces doors, begging the guy to help him due to sympathy. He succeeds the check, and the Councilor gives him the information.<br /> <br /> Does he then make the &quot;Clue roll&quot; to determine the usefulness of the clue in order to get his elements? Is the Clue roll intended as an abstraction of this whole process?<br /> <br /> I'd love your thoughts, guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 12-14-2015, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T09:50:46-08:00","id":786766,"title":"","content":"By-the-book I think you would roll for the Clue at that point, as things like the character's personal stakes in the investigation and so on could be factors.<br /> <br /> Like, it's possible to get the guy to talk (succeed on Social maneuvers) and then have the investigator's questioning produce bad results (for example, they get hit by the suggested penalty to the Clue roll for being emotionally invested, and so when the councilor talks they hear what they <i>want </i>to hear or they have to cut the interview short because the investigator gets too agitated and the councilor gets threatened.)<br /> <br /> My gut instinct would be that I wouldn't want to call for a clue roll after at least two rolls for Social Maneuvering and maybe a third to just get the meeting. Just have the force-doors roll &quot;work as&quot; the Uncover Clues roll.<br /> <br /> Offhand I'd have handled that scene like this. The parenthetical stuff is analogies to similar plot structures.<br /> 1.) Action to secure meeting<br /> (Chase scene to catch fleeing accomplice, larceny roll to break into someone's office)<br /> <br /> 2.) Go to meeting, make Uncover Clue roll using a Social Skill to model the interview/interrogation process. Even if the guy won't give you the information you're looking for, he might accidentally reveal something or compromise and point you in a useful direction. On a dramatic failure, he misleads you. This avoids &quot;he won't talk at all&quot;, the least useful possibility, as a potential outcome.<br /> (Interrogate the suspect in the interview room, search the desk for incriminating documents)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":". 12-15-2015, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T12:45:19-08:00","id":786866,"title":"","content":"I agree with Five Eyes, I would consolidate the Forcing Doors attempt and the Uncover Clues attempt into a single roll. So it would suffer penalties both from the number of doors remaining and the number of times the character had used that dice pool to uncover clues in this investigation, and could benefit both from Hard Leverage and from spending Elements, as well as any Merits the character may have that interact with either subsystem. Then the possible results would be:<br /> <br /> - Dramatic Failure: The Councilor resents the character's attempts to draw information out of him. He offers false information (a Tainted Clue) and is immune to further Social Maneuvering attempts from that character. The character may gain a negative Condition, like Guilty or Notoriety.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Failure: The Councilor is resistant to the character's attempts to draw information out of him. They're still able to draw some insight from his terse responses, but not as much as they had hoped (an Incomplete Clue). He is immune to further Social Maneuvering attempts from that character. <br /> <br /> - Success: The character manages to tease the information they're looking for out of the Councilor (a Clue). He will still be susceptible to further Social Maneuvering attempts by that character.<br /> <br /> - Exceptional Success: The Councilor is especially responsive to the character's attempts. He spills everything he knows (a Clue with an extra Element) and is still susceptible to future Sociap Maneuvering attempts by that character. The character may gain a beneficial Condition like Informed or Connected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T12:54:39-08:00","id":786869,"title":"","content":"I hope someone's posted a need for clarification in the errata thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:08:19-08:00","id":786881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=786869#post786869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope someone's posted a need for clarification in the errata thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's been brought up there too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T01:06:08-08:00","id":789157,"title":"","content":"I've had a lot of trouble figuring this mechanic out. I found the social system with the doors to be very similar. My experience with that was that it was very difficult to understand just from reading it, but as soon as we used it everything became much clearer. I'm hoping it will be the same with this one.<br /> <br /> I'm going to be running a game that is inspired by the heist genre, so I'm wondering if I can modify this into some sort of 'planning' system where they use it to plan out their heist and gain bonuses. Not sure yet whether it will work that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T06:21:01-08:00","id":789225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=789157#post789157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to be running a game that is inspired by the heist genre, so I'm wondering if I can modify this into some sort of 'planning' system where they use it to plan out their heist and gain bonuses. Not sure yet whether it will work that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check <b>Crafting Rules</b>, on page 100 of <b>CoD</b> - I literally just read them, and they mark you can make &quot;heist plans&quot; like <b>GTA San Andreas</b> <i>Four Dragons Casino</i> missions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I made a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/789226-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-building-equipemnt-crafting-rules-examples-in-cod\"><b>third</b></a> topic on examples of those in play also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-22-2015, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T08:08:03-08:00","id":789263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=789157#post789157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had a lot of trouble figuring this mechanic out. I found the social system with the doors to be very similar. My experience with that was that it was very difficult to understand just from reading it, but as soon as we used it everything became much clearer. I'm hoping it will be the same with this one.<br /> <br /> I'm going to be running a game that is inspired by the heist genre, so I'm wondering if I can modify this into some sort of 'planning' system where they use it to plan out their heist and gain bonuses. Not sure yet whether it will work that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would. I'm planning a Demon game based off of the show Scandal where the Demons are reputation fixers, and will be using the Investigation system in a similar manner. Each roll represents something the players may do help someone, but otherwise it works the exact same.For yours, it would just represent each stage of the plan. Alternatively, if they are trying to evade security throughout the heist, you could use a modified version of the chase rules. <br /> <br /> I have to say that I love these rules. They don't just make sense from a Storytelling perspective, they make sense as pedagogy too. Its awesome to see!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:52:45-08:00","id":789379,"title":"","content":"Oh great, it sounds like I'm going to have a lot of useful tools for this chronicle. Now I just need to figure out how to use them all. Thanks Wyrdhamster and Second Chances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T11:10:45-08:00","id":805358,"title":"","content":"Reading the whole rules once again I think <b>you can <i>Uncover the Truth</i> with less than needed Clues - you just need to have &lt;base Clues number&gt; of Elements</b>. See those quotes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronicles of Darkness, p. 79</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once characters reach the required number of Clues, they\u2019re able to Uncover the Truth if that\u2019s their goal. They can do so without any additional rolls if they spend a number of Clue elements (divided however they like) equal to the<br /> required Clues for the investigation. See below for more on <i>Uncovering the Truth</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronicles of Darkness, p. 81</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once characters have the requisite Clues, they may Uncover the Truth. So long as they have the required number of Clues, this doesn\u2019t require a roll; they have pieced together the puzzle. However, for every Clue short of the required<br /> total, the Storyteller adds one significant complication to the investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in mine <b>Yellow Sign Investigation</b> example - if character has only 5 Clues and 5 Elements from them, they <b>cannot</b> <i>Uncover the Truth</i>. ( They could make <i>Castle Theory Roll</i> by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=785838#post785838\">mine own House Rule</a>, but it still be on -8 penalty ). But if they have 5 Clues and 13 Elements - the same number of Elements that base Clues need to Solve the Mystery - they can <i>Uncover the Truth with Complications</i>, based on 8 Clues missing.<br /> <br /> This is how I understand the system for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T21:20:27-08:00","id":805773,"title":"","content":"One thing that need a clarification -<b> Is a penalty on re-using the same Skill on particular character? Or on the whole Investigation?</b><br /> <br /> The quote from the corebook point's rather to the second:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronicles of Darkness, p. 79</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dice pool depends on how the characters approach the pursuit. Each time the same Skill is used to uncover Clues in an investigation, the dice pool suffers a cumulative -1 penalty. A diverse, holistic approach always helps in investigations. Continuing with the same approach offers diminishing returns.</div> </div> </div> </div>For example - My players cabal of mages are uncovering <i>Yellow Sign</i> Intruder. As they are mages, all of them have Occult Skill. Our conspiracy theorist Alom is making Occult Skill roll on <i>Uncovering Clue</i>. After his roll, other member of cabal can make the Uncovering Clue roll - this time our psychatrist Ik - and once again on Occult Skill based. <b>Does Ik should have -1 penalty on reusing Occult Skill or no?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:25:47-07:00","id":1240586,"title":"","content":"I'm quite sleep deprived, so I'll come back to this tomorrow for another go through and try to understand this better, but for now, my big question is whether this tool as written is meant just to flesh out minor investigations (where'd character X go to based on their tossed apartment? What can we glean from the crime scene? Etc), or could it in theory be fleshed into a multi session mystery (for example if I wanted to convert a Gumshoe scenario)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T16:33:59-07:00","id":1240634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baileyborough</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784983-cofd-corebook-how-to-run-investigations-and-clues?p=1240586#post1240586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite sleep deprived, so I'll come back to this tomorrow for another go through and try to understand this better, but for now, my big question is whether this tool as written is meant just to flesh out minor investigations (where'd character X go to based on their tossed apartment? What can we glean from the crime scene? Etc), or could it in theory be fleshed into a multi session mystery (for example if I wanted to convert a Gumshoe scenario)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be as short or long as you need. Larger require Clue totals will extend the Investigation, with really small totals being suited for one or two Scene Investigations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}